							</td>
							<td width="75%" align="left">
								&nbsp;<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php#1">General Category</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=1.0">General Discussion</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1479.60#msg15680">Re: Class - Re-envisionments</a>
							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: March 19, 2005, 07:27:18 pm
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">I have no idea why some clerics think that getting an invis spell is so important. I have been using Cloudy Potions for 3 years now and have NEVER died using them. Well except once with a see-invis mob that I had not spotted. Just buy a backpack full of them, and have one in a clickabel slot.  Watch your chat screen for the becoming visible message, find a safe spot, and insta-click yourself back to a no-seeum. Padding through HoH, I see lots of invis-casting characters die between basements cause they dont have time to cast the spell before they get whooped. <br /><br />Now, I have never even loaded my undead spells because, frankly, in a group they are not that great compared to real damage dealers. So, the new improvements are no help there. And previous cleric poster are correct - where the hell can you use them? What I want is MITIGATION. It does me no good to have a ton of HP if a mob can hit me for near max every time. Whether at 4K or 9K - I will go down. Whether it is 2 seconds or 5 seconds does not make a ton of difference. Mitigation would at least let me last until a real plate class can gain aggro. In addition, I might ever be able to solo some very very light blues, which now is but a dream.<br /><br />The Rev<br />Archon of Outcast Adventurers</td>
						</tr>
