							</td>
							<td width="75%" align="left">
								&nbsp;<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php#1">General Category</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=1.0">General Discussion</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1103.0#msg11000">Re: Removal of the Shaman Class!</a>
							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: September 09, 2004, 09:57:56 pm
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">While I can agree with some of the points above, I can easily disagree with others. First, you are right about the DoTs. These are supposedly the defining attribute of the class, and they are next to useless, and sometimes downright dangerous in higher level zones. But as a Cleric, I can tell you that the difference between Shaman slows and those of enchanters and beastlords is very noticible. As for heals, I would kill to have Quiescense in my arsenal. It has way more bang for the buck than the cleric HoTs.<br /><br />Revenos Aurelios<br />65th Archon of Outcast Adventurers</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td colspan="3" class="windowbg2" align="right">
							</td>
						</tr>
					</table>
				</td>
			</tr>
		</table>
		<table border="0" width="85%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="0" class="bordercolor" align="center">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table border="0" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" class="bordercolor" align="center">
						<tr class="titlebg">
							<td align="left" style="padding: 0 1ex;">
								13
							</td>
							<td width="75%" align="left">
								&nbsp;<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php#1">General Category</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?board=1.0">General Discussion</a> / <a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1016.30#msg10234">Re: Future of EQ</a>
							</td>
							<td align="right" style="padding: 0 1ex; white-space: nowrap;">
								on: August 19, 2004, 10:52:44 am
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">I don&#039;t understand where all the angst is coming from at mobs becoming trivial. So what? When you got to fighting the birds in South Karana, the Throne Room in Crushbone was trivial too.&nbsp; This is called progression. It is part of the game and has been since day one. I agree with one of the previous posters that the magic of a new thing is dulled with time and experience, and can never be regained. The problem is that by now, the new mobs will be tougher, but you will still fight them in much the same way as you fought the bandits in Oasis. The basic mechanisms of the game are not going to change that drastically, so the factors of the unknown that you relished as a true newbie will not have the same intensity. In a way, we are all like children who cannot wait to grow up, but when we are grown, long for those simple days of childhood. Sux, huh.<br /><br />Revenos Aurelios<br />65th Archon of Outcast Adventurers</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td colspan="3" class="windowbg2" align="right">
							</td>
						</tr>
					</table>
				</td>
